<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold seen mixed after budget.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold seen mixed after budget.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold prices are likely to remain mixed this week after Finance Minister Sartaj Aziz told Reuters on Friday he foresaw no early downward adjustment of the rupee, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>Gold prices are likely to fluctuate in a narrow band during the week on speculative buying, one Karachi dealer said, adding that low demand would keep silver prices steady.</p>
<p>Weekly prices:</p>
<p>							 Saturday   June 7</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grams   4,638	4,685</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   6,600	6,600</p>
<p>($1 = 40.49 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
